# A mana ability can be activated whenever its controller has priority (CR 605.3a, 117.1): in Bot2's upkeep Bot1 sacrifices a
# Lotus Petal for red mana and casts Lightning Bolt with it, in a turn that is not its own. The sacrificed Petal stays in
# the graveyard and the mana is used up (CR 106.4); the Petal cannot be used again.

[Bot1 Deck]
Lotus Petal
Lightning Bolt
Island x5
Island x12

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Lotus Petal.Cast
Bot1.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Upkeep]
Bot1.Battlefield.Lotus Petal.Activate(Color: Red)
Bot1.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot2)
Bot1.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
! Bot1.Battlefield.Lotus Petal.Activate

[Expect]
Bot2.Life = 17
Bot1.Graveyard = Lightning Bolt; Lotus Petal
Bot1.Battlefield.Count = 0
